{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792693326,"nonce":"GbUgagdXhYthinUi0Xpb8lFvm9g=","title":"Ignore offset-only locations when building editor indexes","message":"After parameter locations were recorded during lowering, compiler bootstrap symbols could have a known file ID and byte offset with unknown line and column (both zero). FileSymbolIndex accepted these as editor positions because SourceLocation::is_valid only checks the file ID. Converting the index to zero-based LSP coordinates then underflowed, aborting the persisted index build. This broke completion and prevented BLADE reuse on subsequent opens.\n\nThe protocol run in /tmp/rayzor-lsp-coverage-tests2.log exposed this in nine existing sessions, including initialization macros, completion, and cache restart coverage. The fix filters out locations lacking one-based line/column coordinates at index construction and uses checked conversion at serialization. A focused unit regression covers offset-only and usable locations. Validation is in progress against the current branch, preserving the subsequent worker-side persisted-index request fix.","files":null}]}